"""Fifty complete independent original-field readings, frozen before candidate inspection."""
NOTES = {}


def note(number, language, text):
    key = ('deenhindi-bukhari:' + number, language)
    assert key not in NOTES
    NOTES[key] = text


note('1487', 'hi', 'The complete Hindi supplies Jabir’s Messenger-attributed prohibition of selling fruit before ripeness becomes clear. The multi-step prefatory transmission route is source context; retain the coherent final attribution/body and the complete until-ripeness limitation. Do not supply a sale example or external legal explanation.')
note('1487', 'ur', 'I read the whole Urdu chain and actual prohibition independently. Separate the pure prefatory route, preserve Jabir’s source attribution and every word of the ripeness-until condition. The source’s punctuation and plural references remain exact.')
note('1489', 'hi', 'Separate the pure opening route. Ibn Umar reports Umar’s donated horse, wish to repurchase and the Messenger’s do-not-take-back reply. The following Ibn Umar habit of donating any repurchased charity is a separate actual Companion practice, not Prophetic speech. The final parenthesis explicitly explains non-use and chapter/hadith correspondence and is compiler context in full.')
note('1489', 'ur', 'The whole Urdu supplies Umar’s horse episode and the separately narrated Ibn Umar repurchase/re-donation practice. Keep their own voices and complete actual actions. The final non-use/chapter-correspondence parenthesis is explanatory apparatus, and the multi-step opening route is context. No missing horse price or donor identity is inferred.')
note('1493', 'hi', 'The opening multi-step route remains context before Aisha’s actual account. The Barirah purchase/emancipation/wala dialogue and the later meat/charity/gift exchange are two distinct supplied report families. The short jo bandi thin status apposition explains what purchase-for-emancipation already states and can be context. Preserve the contractual condition, source identities and every actual reply.')
note('1493', 'ur', 'I independently read the full two-part Urdu. Separate the transmission prefix and the inserted slave-status apposition. Preserve the actual purchase/retained-wala condition and emancipation reply, then the separately introduced meat exchange and charity/gift distinction under their actual voices. Do not merge the two report scenes into one continuous Prophetic speech.')
note('1500', 'hi', 'The prefatory route and its Urwah father-identity insertion are context. Abu Humayd’s actual report appoints the source-named Abdullah ibn Lutbiyah of Banu Asad to collect Banu Sulaym zakat and states the later accounting. Keep all named groups and the complete finite appointment/return/accounting body without outside name correction.')
note('1500', 'ur', 'The complete Urdu supplies Abu Humayd’s appointment/accounting report with the same actual groups and named collector. The long transmitter route and parenthetic father identification are separate source context. Preserve the printed لتبیہ form and all actual events rather than replacing them with another edition’s name.')
note('1501', 'hi', 'The whole source reports the Uraynah group’s illness, permission regarding camels, murder/theft, pursuit and punishment. Keep all supplied actions as historical source content, not present medical or legal advice. The disease-exclusive-cure parenthesis is explanatory justification and the final support-route list is apparatus. The those-camels herdsman qualifier limits the participant relation and remains. I initially retain the heat-severity causal qualifier as the supplied immediate event cause. Separate the multi-step opening route; preserve all original defects.')
note('1501', 'ur', 'I read every Urdu action and qualifier. The initial chain, disease/only-cure justification and final Abu Qilabah/Thabit/Humayd support routes belong to context. The herdsman’s these-camels relation materially identifies the narrated victim; the heat-severity qualifier supplies the immediate narrative cause and initially remains. The violent and medical details are exact attributed historical wording, not endorsed instructions or a verified treatment claim.')
note('1502', 'hi', 'Separate the prefatory transmission route. Anas brings Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah for tahnik and actually observes the branding tool and zakat-camel branding. The parenthetic yani mouth/chewing definition explains tahnik and is context; do not turn the definition into a separately witnessed action absent from the report. Keep the actual purpose and observed scene.')
note('1502', 'ur', 'The own Urdu supplies the visit’s tahnik purpose and the contemporaneous branding-tool/camel scene. The long route and explicit yani definition are context. The finite observation remains Anas’s report; no performance of tahnik is manufactured from the glossary.')
note('1503', 'hi', 'The multi-step route is context before Ibn Umar’s actual report of the Messenger’s fitr obligation. Preserve the one-saa alternatives, all named classes of Muslims and the deadline before going to prayer. Sadqa-e-fitr is a duplicate noun gloss of fitr-zakat and can be context. Eid materially specifies which prayer and must remain selected, unlike that synonym.')
note('1503', 'ur', 'I read the complete Urdu obligation, categories, quantities and timing. Separate the chain and duplicate صدقہ فطر gloss. Retain the عید qualification because it supplies the actual prayer/deadline domain; all other source scope and classes remain unchanged.')
note('1505', 'hi', 'The opening multi-step chain is context. Abu Said explicitly reports the community’s practice of giving one saa of barley as charity. This own field does not expressly name a Prophetic speaker or a festival; classify the finite Companion collective practice without importing those missing qualifications.')
note('1505', 'ur', 'The full Urdu supplies Abu Said’s first-person-plural one-saa barley-charity practice. Keep that actual source-attributed practice after separating the prefatory chain. Do not label it a direct Prophetic saying or add a fitr occasion merely from neighboring records.')
note('1506', 'hi', 'The long prefatory route ends in hearing Abu Said; retain his coherent saying/body with every printed food alternative and measure. The parenthetic dry-grapes-or-figs phrase is a lexical explanation of zabib and remains context, without correcting its unusual definition. The unparenthesized grain-or-wheat alternative remains exactly supplied.')
note('1506', 'ur', 'I read Abu Said’s whole list and its actual one-saa alternatives. Separate the transmission prefix and the خشک انگور یا انجیر glossary, preserving its source defect in context. The actual communal fitr practice is a Companion report; the printed grain/wheat and all other alternatives remain literal.')
note('1507', 'hi', 'Separate the multi-step route. The Messenger’s supplied one-saa date/barley command and Ibn Umar’s later statement that people adopted two mudd of wheat are distinct actual voices/reports. The half-saa parenthesis converts the already supplied two-mudd amount and is context; retain the actual two-mudd measure and people’s later practice.')
note('1507', 'ur', 'The Urdu contains the Prophetic command and a separately attributed Ibn Umar report of people’s later equivalence practice. Keep both under their own speakers. The آدھا صاع parenthesis is a unit-conversion explanation, not a new spoken quantity, while the original two-mudd statement remains. The prefatory chain is context.')
note('1510', 'hi', 'Separate only the prefatory route. Abu Said reports a one-saa contribution on Eid al-Fitr in the Prophet’s time and then names their actual foods. The food-grain object qualifies what is measured and must remain. The in-those-days parenthesis restricts the historical food description and initially remains. The second food statement is Abu Said’s own supplied explanation, not unattributed compiler prose or a Prophetic utterance.')
note('1510', 'ur', 'I fully read the two Abu Said statements. Preserve the Prophet-era festival setting, material object of the one-saa amount and the temporal qualification of their food list. Keep the actual named foods and no modern conversion. The opening chain remains separate context; the attributed food statement remains a Companion saying.')
note('1511', 'hi', 'The opening chain is context. Keep the supplied fitr-or-Ramadan wording uncertainty, obligation, categories and sab-par scope. The later half-saa practice, Ibn Umar’s dates/barley substitution, contributions for children, recipients and early giving are actual reported practices under a later reporting voice. The two explicitly introduced Imam Bukhari explanations—my-sons identity and collection/distribution interpretation—are compiler context in full. Do not silently make the unmarked my-sons voice Prophetic or transfer the compiler’s identification into an unqualified body attribution.')
note('1511', 'ur', 'The full Urdu contains a Prophetic obligation followed by later communal/Ibn Umar practices. Preserve the term alternative, inclusive scope, shortage event, children and early-giving timing. Distinguish the source reporting voice for میرے بیٹوں; the appended Bukhari identification is visible context. His following collection-versus-poor explanation is also compiler apparatus. Separate the prefatory route and both final compiler blocks without deleting actual practice clauses.')
note('1512', 'hi', 'Ibn Umar’s coherent final frame supplies the complete Messenger-attributed one-saa barley/date fitr obligation for the named categories. The multi-step prefatory route is context, while all actual quantity, alternatives and scope remain literal. There is no further compiler tail.')
note('1512', 'ur', 'The own Urdu fully supplies Ibn Umar’s report, the Messenger’s obligation, one-saa alternatives and all categories. Preserve that entire body after separating only the opening multi-step route; no outside timing or definition is added.')
note('1513', 'hi', 'The final Ibn Abbas report supplies Fadl’s seat, the woman’s arrival, mutual looks, the source’s literal wished-to-turn-face wording, her elderly-father question and the affirmative reply. The initial Farewell-Hajj parenthesis repeats the explicit final historical sentence and can be context; keep that final sentence. The badal parenthesis names what on-his-behalf already says and is lexical context. Preserve all real incapacity/representation conditions and do not normalize the source’s action verb.')
note('1513', 'ur', 'I read the whole Urdu scene and dialogue. Separate the route, repeated initial Farewell-Pilgrimage label and بدل terminology gloss; the final historical event statement remains. Keep the exact wanted-to-turn wording, the father’s age/riding incapacity, the on-his-behalf question and yes answer. No missing participant identity is supplied.')
note('1515', 'hi', 'The initial route and final Ibn Abbas/Anas support-transmission notice are context. The actual Jabir report supplies the Messenger’s ihram at Dhu al-Hulayfah when his mount stood upright carrying him. Preserve that complete location/action/timing relation, without adding an omitted Talbiyah formula or other companion version.')
note('1515', 'ur', 'The Urdu independently supplies the same finite ihram/mount-standing report. Retain all its actual timing and place words; separate the multi-step prefix and final supporting-route notice. No body is inferred from the named additional transmitters.')
note('1518', 'hi', 'The shortened opening chain is damaged; do not insert Urdu’s omitted transmitters. The source prints defective ऐसा and तांईं in its actual woman’s complaint, the Prophet’s Abdur Rahman/sister instruction and the subsequent riding/umrah account. Retain those exact defects with qualified source identities/place; do not silently normalize to Aisha/Tanim. Separate only the pure prefatory route, not the actual complaint or resulting actions.')
note('1518', 'ur', 'The complete own Urdu expressly names Aisha and Tanim, with the full initial route. Keep the complaint, Messenger’s instruction to Abdur Rahman concerning his sister, rear-seat ride and completed umrah as actual supplied content. The route is context; Urdu’s names and missing links must not be copied into Hindi.')
note('1520', 'hi', 'The long prefatory chain is context before Aisha’s actual why-do-we-not question and the Messenger’s no/best-jihad-is-mabrur-hajj reply. Preserve the actual we-pronoun scope, negative opening and mabrur term, without adding a definition or expanding the question to an outside category.')
note('1520', 'ur', 'The own Urdu fully supplies Aisha’s question and the Prophet’s qualified reply. Keep all source wording and its pronoun scope after separating the multi-step route. The text is a historical reported exchange, not a new general instruction or a supplied definition of mabrur.')
note('1522', 'hi', 'The initial Malik/Zuhayr route is context, but Zaid ibn Jubayr’s actual visit, residence/canopy scene and question must remain. The parenthetic Zaid reporting resumption identifies the following first-person question and is meaningful attribution. Ibn Umar’s reply explicitly reports the Messenger’s three regional miqat assignments. Preserve the whole scene and no external place normalization.')
note('1522', 'ur', 'I fully read Zaid’s visit and canopy setting, the resumed first-person question and Abdullah’s Prophetic miqat reply. The Zaid attribution parenthesis remains with the actual question, unlike a redundant chain glossary. Separate only the pure prefatory transmission route; keep the actual three region/place pairs as printed.')
note('1523', 'hi', 'Ibn Abbas reports the Yemen pilgrims’ claimed trust, lack of provisions and subsequent begging, followed by the actually supplied verse translation. Keep the historical report and real quoted rendering, without adding a verse number or Arabic. The multi-step prefix and final Ibn Uyaynah/Amr/Ikrama mursal transmission notice remain source context, with the printed criticism preserved.')
note('1523', 'ur', 'The complete Urdu supplies the Yemen/provisions/begging report and the actual translated revelation wording. Retain both as the source’s Ibn Abbas account. Separate the opening route and final mursal route notice; that printed transmission qualification is not an independent authenticity grade and is not discarded.')
note('1526', 'hi', 'After the prefatory route, Ibn Abbas’s report lists four regional miqats, passing-through conditions and pilgrimage intention. Preserve all those actual limits. The final inside-miqat clause is abbreviated before the Mecca instruction; keep the supplied wording without completing a familiar rule from another edition. The actual Mecca-from-Mecca instruction remains.')
note('1526', 'ur', 'I read all four region/place assignments and passing/intention conditions. The source places a full stop after its inner-miqat inhabitants clause before the Mecca instruction; preserve that defective join/abbreviation rather than synthesizing a missing predicate. Only the pure opening route is context, with all actual instructions retained.')
note('1536', 'hi', 'The damaged prefatory route omits names, but bin Umayyah’s actual request to Umar to see revelation must not be swallowed by a chain cut. Keep that request, Jiirnah scene, unnamed man’s perfume/ihram question, the source’s red-face/snoring observation and the three-washes/jubbah/umrah reply exactly. Later Yaala is actually printed; do not retroactively fill the damaged opening name. The final actual I-asked-Ata/yes exchange is separately attributed scholarly dialogue, not another Prophetic utterance; do not externally identify its unmarked questioner.')
note('1536', 'ur', 'The full Urdu route explicitly names Safwan’s father Yaala ibn Umayyah before his actual Umar request. Separate the prefatory chain but retain that finite request and all revelation/cloth/face/snoring/return/question/reply events. The final question to Ata about the three-wash meaning and his yes are an actual later scholarly exchange, with an unmarked resumed questioner and distinct voice. No medical diagnosis or outside story continuation is inserted.')
note('1537', 'hi', 'The short Said ibn Jubayr attribution is coherent report framing, not a long pure preface to strip. The field supplies Ibn Umar’s oiling habit, a later I-mentioned-to-Ibrahim exchange and Aswad’s embedded Aisha report about perfume gleam during ihram. Keep those actual voices and distinct report families; do not turn Ibrahim’s question into a Prophetic saying or merge the habit with Aisha’s separate testimony.')
note('1537', 'ur', 'The full Urdu contains the Ibn Umar habit, the actual Ibrahim dialogue and a separately transmitted Aisha observation. Preserve the short own attribution and the short embedded Aswad/Aisha frame, with the latter’s actual during-ihram limit. No multi-step compiler prefix or new commentary is present to trim; the resumed first-person link remains source-qualified.')
note('1538', 'hi', 'I independently read this complete field despite its literal equality with1537. It remains a distinct occurrence, with the same supplied Ibn Umar habit, Ibrahim dialogue and embedded Aisha perfume report separately classified. Keep the short attribution frames and every actual source word; no identity merge or missing speaker name is inferred.')
note('1538', 'ur', 'This separately numbered Urdu field was read in full. Preserve its distinct occurrence identity and the actual habit/dialogue/Aisha-report voices and families even though the wording equals1537. The short transmitters serve coherent actual attribution; they are not a long prefatory list to delete indiscriminately.')
note('1541', 'hi', 'The two long parallel transmission routes, second-chain label and compiler route introduction precede the only actual report body and remain context. Retain the coherent final he-was-saying frame and the Messenger’s ihram near the Dhu al-Hulayfah mosque. Ibn Umar is named in the source chain/context; no missing name is inserted into the final pronoun wording.')
note('1541', 'ur', 'The full Urdu includes two route lists and no separate finite event before the second. Keep both chains and the second-route label as context, preserving their identities. The actual final saying frame and mosque/location/ihram predicate remain intact, with no added contrast or reconstructed Talbiyah wording.')
note('1543', 'hi', 'The short Ubaydullah/Ibn Abbas introduction is coherent attribution, not a long prefatory route to strip. Preserve Usamah’s Arafat-to-Muzdalifah ride, Fadl’s next leg and Ibn Abbas’s report that both said the Prophet continued Talbiyah until the Aqabah stoning. Keep the two reporters/legs and endpoint explicit, without inventing an uttered formula.')
note('1543', 'ur', 'I read the full own Urdu journey and both-reporters statement. Its short attribution can stay; the two legs and continued-Talbiyah-until-stoning report are actual supplied content. Retain the source’s collective attribution and exact endpoint, with no canonical number or omitted formula supplied.')

assert len(NOTES) == 50
